{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqhg3r9l5iv","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Full automode design: Opus escalation and merge verdict action","summary":"Added config.automode flag (dashboard toggle). Two effects: (1) POST /guidance blocking escalations are resolved by awaiting an Opus CLI subprocess (claude -p ... --model claude-opus-4-8) instead of pausing the loop — the tool call blocks ~30-60s but returns a real answer; (2) new 'merge' verdict action in verdicts.js — when judge completes with {action:'merge', task_key:'<impl>'} AND automode is on, the route handler in overlay.js auto-calls git.mergeBranch. Without automode, merge verdict is recorded but not executed (dispatcher actionable). Judges in automode must include the merge verdict on APPROVE; on KICK BACK use set_status failed with no merge verdict.\n\n**Why:** User needs agents to run fully autonomously without manual direction on escalations or merge approvals.\n\n**How to apply:** Dispatchers set automode via POST /config or dashboard toggle. Judges add merge verdict in complete_task verdicts when approving in automode. Falls back to blocking escalation if Opus CLI unavailable.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-17T02:22:05.001Z","vec":[-0.041954196989536285,-0.036050744354724884,-0.022168004885315895,-0.060706187039613724,0.010584338568150997,0.03723332658410072,0.040213558822870255,0.09100887179374695,0.04117186367511749,0.010249574668705463,0.033664461225271225,0.030320333316922188,-0.08972910046577454,0.00039104092866182327,-0.04470474272966385,0.0503094419836998,0.05971234291791916,-0.04934098571538925,-0.07082811743021011,-0.051560062915086746,-0.008154396899044514,-0.026669278740882874,0.053401779383420944,0.019949406385421753,-0.0016857896698638797,-0.004009165335446596,-0.12424439191818237,-0.0488051176071167,0.03730781748890877,-0.06583806872367859,0.031874291598796844,-0.01740666665136814,-0.05315236747264862,0.017600079998373985,-0.03126213699579239,0.03607957437634468,-0.0401237